3. Reusing the source code

Anyone may reuse the source code of the Software, or any of its components, in
their own applications without prior written permission, provided that all of
the following conditions are met:

  1. Sentinel Blockchain Program only. The Sentinel dVPN is designed to operate
     exclusively with the Sentinel Blockchain Program deployed on the Solana
     blockchain. Neither the reused code nor any application that incorporates
     it may be used with any other blockchain network or dVPN program, or with
     any competing white-label VPN solution. In other words, the Software is for
     building dVPN applications on Sentinel itself, not elsewhere.
  2. Attribution. The application displays the attribution described in
     section 4.
  3. Branding. The application does not use the branding of the Software, except
     in the attribution required by section 4, and does not present itself as an
     official Sentinel application.
  4. Other terms. All other terms of this license are complied with.

4. Attribution

Any reuse of the source code of the Software, or of any of its components,
requires a visible attribution in the derived work (for example, an application
that reuses this code). The attribution must use exactly the following wording:

    Built on Sentinel.

The attribution must be accompanied by a visible link to the Sentinel website:
<https://sentinel.co>.

"Visible" means shown to the users of the derived work, for example on its About
or Credits screen, and not only in its source code.

